 Identity includes the isolate client and the validated component/function path, not an export
-alias or invocation arguments. HTTP actions share their component's router allowance: handler
-selection occurs inside JavaScript, and raw URL paths are not trustworthy admission identities.
+alias or invocation arguments. HTTP actions additionally use the method and registered route
+resolved from deployment analysis before isolate admission. Exact routes have separate allowances;
+all requests matching one prefix share that prefix's allowance. HEAD shares GET's allowance.
+Unmatched requests share one allowance per component router. Raw URL suffixes and query strings
+cannot create admission identities. Different routes still consume the same global action cap;
+route isolation does not reserve capacity for authentication or any other handler.
 The cap does not apply to Node execution, queries, mutations, or ancestor-unblocking descendants.
 
