@@ -288,8 +288,10 @@ mechanism.
 
 The optional `MAX_ISOLATE_ACTION_WORKERS_PER_FUNCTION` bounds each validated function inside the
 global action allowance, including pending initial-permit reservations. It uses client and
-component identity; HTTP routes share their component router. Zero retains the global-only
-policy. Queries, mutations, and ancestor-unblocking descendants are exempt. Selection skips a
+component identity. HTTP actions additionally use the analyzed registered method and route;
+prefix matches share their registered prefix, HEAD shares GET, and unmatched requests share a
+component-router allowance. Concrete URLs never define admission identities. Zero retains the
+global-only policy. Queries, mutations, and ancestor-unblocking descendants are exempt. Selection skips a
 capped function without hiding other eligible work; completion and canceled/expired reservations
 release the function count. See [Action cap](README.md#action-cap) for configuration and limits.
 
